  "_NO_DEPENDENCY_ON_arc_executor": "A16's own design investigation: decomposition needs no ExecClass, no dispatch, no re-arm -- it is graph arithmetic over ArcGoal/ArcTier. Depending on arc_magnitude (and, through it, arc_goals) is sufficient. This keeps MG4 addable/removable independent of the executor line and out of the re-arm/dispatch scope A13-A16 all exclude.",
  "description": "MG4 -- ORDER-N DECOMPOSITION (A16). mg_rung (seeds/arc_magnitude.json) computes decompose_required and names the measured ladder a split would use; nothing consumed it. This seed is the consumer: mg_decompose mints one child ArcGoal per un-materialised tier of the ladder -- EVERY tier, not only the ones affordable under the CURRENT horizon (a first draft gated on in_horizon and was corrected before shipping: decompose_required==1.0 and in_horizon(any tier) are mutually exclusive by construction on this ladder's monotonic cost, which would have made the gated rule permanently dead under its own trigger -- see this builder's docstring) -- each child carrying its tier's raw increment_n as headroom_n and the tier's own survival factor alongside it, then individually re-priced by the UNCHANGED mg_rung against the same horizon (6.3's own point: a cheap tier can become actionable even when the whole ladder was not). mg_decompose_retire moves the parent to a DESCRIPTIVE terminal status ('decomposed') and, load-bearingly, zeroes its headroom_n -- which is what actually excludes it from ag_select's AND mg_select's pool, via POOL()'s own pre-existing Gt(headroom_n, 0.0) clause, with ZERO edits to seeds/arc_goals.json. Retirement fires only once EVERY tier has been materialised as a child and at least one child exists, never on the flag alone. mg_child_order_n gives each child its own discounted order-N headroom (headroom_n * tier_survival), which seeds/arc_magnitude.json v1.1.0's ONE additive guard on mg_goal_order_n_default protects from being silently overwritten -- otherwise the SAME inflation trap decision 2 guards against on the mint side would re-appear on the pricing side every fixpoint pass. FOLD-UP IS NOT TWINNED and NO ExecClass IS ADDED -- named out of scope in A16, not silently dropped. THE HONEST CONSEQUENCE OF DECISION 2's CORRECTION: the registered arithmetic identity (Sum(children.headroom_n*tier_survival)==parent.orderN_headroom_n) holds on a CONSTRUCTED scene (decompose_required forced with no horizon truncating the parent's own reading) but NOT on the natural push_back trigger, where the parent's own orderN_headroom_n is horizon-truncated to 0 while the children correctly sum to the ladder's full projected value -- measured and reported, not hidden, in PROGRAM_SYNTHESIS_ARC6_MG4_DECOMPOSE.md.",
  "microtheory": {
    "name": "arc_goal_decomposition",
    "description": "A huge goal is not one atomic unit with one discounted headroom -- it is a measured tier ladder, already graph data, already keyed by a measured population join. Decomposition is the projection of that existing object into goals, each re-priced INDEPENDENTLY against the same horizon the parent could not fit \u2014 so a cheap tier can become individually actionable even when the whole ladder was not."
  },
